COMPONENTS

Everything a computer can use is a component: its parts (gpu,
filesystem, eeprom, modem, redstone), and blocks on its network or
linked to it (screen, keyboard, disk_drive, inventory, tank, energy).

  for address, type in component.list() do print(address, type) end
  local gpu = component.proxy(component.list("gpu")())
  component.gpu          -- the primary gpu (OS only)
  component.invoke(address, "method", ...)
  component.methods(address)  component.doc(address, "method")

The `components -l -d` program lists them with documentation.
Methods marked * run on the server thread and take a tick.
